  "_comment": "Roll-up concepts for the domains conditions.json does not cover. Without these, concept_ancestor contained rows only for conditions and drug ingredients, so 'every lab in the renal panel' or 'any acute care visit' could not be expressed as a descendant query and every phenotype had to enumerate leaf concept ids by hand - which is exactly the portability problem synthetic data is supposed to let you rehearse. Every leaf listed in members gets an edge to its grouper; vocabulary.py then computes the full transitive closure, so an ancestor row exists for every (ancestor, descendant) pair at every distance, not just parent-child. Leaves absent from members roll up to the domain root directly.",

